---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const mode = import.meta.env.MODE;
const flyporter = mode === "prod" ? "htpps://flyporter.com" : "/";
---

<Layout>
  <!-- professional -->
  <section class="paragraph">
    <h1>
      <a
        href="https://orennia.com"
        class="orennia"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        ><span>orennia</span> <span class="green">✦</span></a
      >
    </h1>
    <p>
      I am currently a UX/UI Developer at Orennia, flourishing in a space where
      design and code come together to create beautiful user experiences.
    </p>
    <p>
      What excites me about the renewable energy sector is the opportunity to
      uncover abstractions inside massive datasets and present them in a way
      that helps educate people about their impact. Data visualization is an
      exciting field that blends creativity and complex information into
      something understandable and fun.
    </p>
    <p>
      Fostering a deeper understanding of our role in this world is the first
      step. Protect our planet, support efforts that move the needle, and know
      you're contributing to something greater.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="paragraph">
    <h1>
      <a href="https://flyporter.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        ><span>porter airlines</span> <span class="red">✦</span></a
      >
    </h1>
    <p>
      My first professional role in the industry was as a UX/UI Developer at
      Porter Airlines, helping implement and enhance various UI components
      across the website. I strived to reflect the pleasant flying experience
      into the digital space, turning brand values into great UX/UI.
    </p>
    <p>
      My contributions have helped position the company as a regular industry
      competitor in the aviation field. Being able to support the company's
      expansion from a regional presence to a North American competitor has been
      a rewarding journey.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="paragraph">
    <h1>neo culture studios</h1>
    <p>
      Neo Culture Studios is a freelance company started by me and a close
      colleague, envisioned with helping family businesses initiate and
      revitalize their online presence. Practical design, seamless development,
      and prominent branding from the ground up were our promises kept for
      clients. From first ideation to final delivery, we ensured their visions
      were translated into polished, cohesive products.
    </p>
    <p>
      The responsibilities of a small business helped translate immensely to my
      growth in career and character. I developed many important skills: sincere
      professionalism, tracking deadlines, taking accountability, setting
      worthwhile goals, and having the courage to blindly dive into the deep
      end.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="paragraph">
    <span>--</span>
  </section>

  <!-- personal -->
  <section class="paragraph">
    <h1>chaisweets</h1>
    <p>
      A non-profit freelance project I proposed for a relative's local business.
      Working closely with them, I designed a full website in Figma to showcase
      the brand's elegant dessert selection for special occasions and catering.
      My goal was to expand beyond social media into a more established digital
      presence while reduce friction in the ordering operations.
    </p>
    <p>
      This was my first non-academic and professional pursuit to performing user
      research, creating low-fidelity wireframes, and scheduling regular check
      ups with a client. The amount of work that goes into a design system and
      high-fidelity prototypes can feel everlasting, but the end result after
      over 100+ drafts is worth it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="paragraph">
    <h1>
      <a
        href="https://v1.shwong.world"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        ><span>portfolio v1</span> <span class="red">✦</span></a
      >
    </h1>
    <p>
      First website iteration to showcase my work, designed in Figma and
      developed in React, Next.js, and SCSS. My main design principles to follow
      for the portfolio were minimalism, composure, and fluidity. I was inspired
      by whitespace to create a calming flow for the eyes to follow, resulting
      in simple iconography and a monochromatic pallete. For personality, I
      included a hint of my favourite color - red.
    </p>
    <p>
      The most important thing I learned from this project was how to
      encapsulating a theme, understand scope, and focus on sticking with your
      core intentions. There are seemingly infinite alternatives or improvements
      or new features we can add, but we need to focus on what we're really
      trying to capture.
    </p>
    <p>There's always time to develop another version.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-40);
  }
</style>
